Ultar: matrix-vector path for 9 to 16 tokens (speculative decoding verify blocks)

llama.cpp's Vulkan backend switches from the matrix-vector kernels to the tiled matrix kernels
above 8 tokens. On the Intel Arc 140T (Xe-LPG+, Mesa, integer dot product, no matrix cores) the
tiled kernels are slow for few tokens: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B pp10 32, pp12 38, pp16 46 t/s against
pp8 73. With the vector path up to 16 (experts and dense weights): pp10 79, pp12 85, pp16 92 t/s;
pp1-8 and pp24/32 unchanged; test-backend-ops MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID pass. Verify blocks of
speculative decoding (DFlash: 7-15 drafted tokens) fall exactly into this range.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@
     bool transfer_only;
 };
 
-static constexpr uint32_t mul_mat_vec_max_cols = 8;
+static constexpr uint32_t mul_mat_vec_max_cols = 16;
 
 static constexpr uint32_t p021_max_gqa_ratio = 8;
 
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
